Title: SIGNAL FIRES
Credit: Written for
Author: TRUE STORY system testing
Draft date: 2026-08-19
Notes: Entirely fictional test material. All people, organisations, events, and creative works named below were invented for this test.

====

TITLE CARD: THIS IS A TRUE STORY.

FADE IN:

EXT. NORTHBRIDGE FERRY TERMINAL - DAWN - 2024

Rain crosses an empty terminal. A mural of a silver whale covers the wall.
Beside it hangs a poster of Captain Eliza Vale crossing a black sea.

DR. MAYA ROWAN, forty-two, steps from a taxi carrying a red archive box.
She checks a message from @NorthbridgeWatch and calls 202-555-0147.

MAYA
I arrived at 6:12 this morning. The ferry was already gone.

JONAH REED, fifty, approaches in a Northbridge Transit jacket.

JONAH
You were dismissed from the Oceanic Safety Board in March 2023.

MAYA
That is false. I resigned on April 18, 2023.

JONAH
You also destroyed the inspection report.

MAYA
I preserved three copies and delivered one to Parliament.

INT. NORTHBRIDGE TRANSIT OFFICE - MORNING

A Vela Motors coffee mug sits beneath the registered NORTHBRIDGE TRANSIT logo.
An employee opens https://northbridge-transit.example on a cracked laptop.

DIRECTOR HELEN CROSS enters. She wears a distinctive blue compass tattoo.

HELEN
The Dawn Star carried 312 passengers on its final voyage.

MAYA
The manifest lists 287 passengers and fourteen crew.

HELEN
Maya accepted a fifty-thousand-dollar payment to stay silent.

MAYA
I have never accepted money from Northbridge Transit.

JONAH
Everyone in this city knows you are impossible to work with.

MAYA
That is your opinion, not a fact.

Helen points to a framed photograph of the Dawn Star in heavy seas.

HELEN
That photograph was taken by Luis Ortega on 9 June 2019.

INT. RECORDS ROOM - LATER

Maya unlocks cabinet 4B. The radio plays "Midnight Signal" by The Harbour Lights.

MAYA
The safety audit found corrosion in six load-bearing beams.

JONAH
You told the Herald, "The ship was a disaster waiting to happen."

MAYA
I said, "The inspection process was a disaster." Quote me correctly.

She removes a report titled THE NORTHBRIDGE MARITIME INQUIRY, published in 2021.

MAYA (CONT'D)
The inquiry held twelve public hearings between May and August 2021.

HELEN
No court ever found this company criminally responsible.

EXT. 88 HARBOUR ROAD - NORTHBRIDGE - NIGHT

Protesters gather outside the terminal. A news van shows plate NBR-204.
Someone has painted the Northbridge Transit logo onto a burning life ring.

REPORTER
Dr. Rowan, did Helen Cross order staff to alter the maintenance records?

MAYA
I saw her signature on the amended record. I did not see her alter it.

REPORTER
Is it true Jonah Reed was convicted of fraud in 2018?

JONAH
No. The charge was withdrawn, and that claim has followed me for years.

INT. COMMUNITY HALL - NIGHT

Maya addresses residents beneath a projected film clip from the fictional
documentary Beneath the Wake.

MAYA
The original inspection is missing. The surviving copies conflict.

HELEN
Then you cannot honestly claim to know which copy is authentic.

MAYA
Correct. That question remains unresolved.

JONAH
For what it is worth, I think Maya is brave.

MAYA
That is also an opinion.

EXT. NORTHBRIDGE FERRY TERMINAL - SUNRISE

The terminal doors open. Maya places the red archive box on the public desk.

TITLE CARD: The fictional inquiry reopened on 3 February 2025.

TITLE CARD: No finding had been issued when this story was completed.

FADE OUT.

THE END
